Dear Colleagues,

We are upgrading our CyberArk environment to the new CyberArk Identity Platform. This change is part of our ongoing effort to improve security, simplify access, and provide a more reliable experience for everyone who uses CyberArk.

This message explains what is changing, when it is happening, how it affects you, and what you need to do.

1. What is changing?

We are moving from our current CyberArk Standard Platform to the new CyberArk Identity Platform.

In practical terms, this means:

A new login page / URL to access CyberArk

A more modern, unified portal for accessing privileged accounts and sessions

Improved integration with our corporate identity (SSO / MFA)

Behind-the-scenes enhancements to security, resilience, and performance

Your existing privileged accounts and safes will be migrated into this new platform. The way you log in and launch sessions may look slightly different, but the purpose and capabilities remain the same.

2. What are the benefits for you?

Once the migration is complete, you can expect:

Simpler login experience

Single Sign-On (SSO) where applicable

Consistent use of our corporate Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)

Faster, more reliable access to accounts and sessions

Modern interface with clearer navigation

A platform that is better aligned with Zero Trust and least privilege best practices

3. Key dates & timeline

Migration window: <Date & Time Range – e.g., Saturday, January 11, 2025, 09:00–17:00 (local time)>

Service impact: During this window:

Access to the current CyberArk Standard Platform may be intermittent or unavailable.

After the migration, you will start using the new Identity Platform URL.

We recommend that you avoid scheduling high-risk changes or maintenance activities that depend on CyberArk during this window.

4. What will change for how I log in?

After the migration:

New Portal URL:

Current: https://<old-portal-url>

New: https://<new-identity-portal-url>

Please update your bookmarks after the migration.

Login Method:

You will sign in using your corporate username and password

You may be prompted for MFA (e.g., mobile app push, SMS, token, etc.) as part of the new Identity Platform

If you currently use PSM/PSMP/RDP/SSH shortcuts, RemoteApps, or integrated tools, the way you launch may look slightly different, but the workflow will remain similar. We will provide short guides (with screenshots) for the most common use cases.

5. What do I need to do?

Before the migration:

Complete / check in any critical work that depends on CyberArk.

Close active privileged sessions before the migration window starts.

Note any business-critical scripts or tools that rely on CyberArk so you can test them afterward.

After the migration:

Use the new Identity Platform URL: https://<new-identity-portal-url>

Sign in with your corporate credentials and MFA, if prompted.

Confirm you can:

See your usual Safes

Access your privileged accounts

Launch sessions (RDP/SSH/SQL, etc.) as usual

If anything is missing or not working, please report it immediately (see Support section below).

6. What is not changing?

Your role and permissions in CyberArk are not changing as part of this migration.

The underlying privileged accounts, safes, and policies remain the same (they are simply hosted on the new platform).

Our security controls (session recording, password rotation, approvals where applicable) remain in place.

7. Impact to automated processes & integrations

If your team uses CyberArk for automated password retrieval or integrations (e.g., applications calling CyberArk via CCP/API/Identity Connector):

We will be validating and updating connection settings so they point to the new platform endpoints.

Some integration URLs, certificates, or connection methods may change behind the scenes; the IAM/CyberArk team will coordinate with you if your application is impacted.

Action for application owners:

Be prepared to perform post-migration testing to ensure your integrations are functioning as expected.

Look out for a separate, more technical communication with specific details if your application is affected.

8. Support & contact details

If you have any questions or encounter issues during or after the migration, please contact:

CyberArk / IAM Support Team: <Shared mailbox or ticketing queue – e.g. cyberark-support@company.com
>

