Phone / On-call: <Number, if applicable>

When reporting an issue, please include:

Your username

Date & time of the issue

Steps you were taking (e.g., “launching RDP to server X from Safe Y”)

Any error messages / screenshots

9. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)

Q1. Will I lose any access during this migration?
A. Your access is not being removed. However, during the migration window, CyberArk may be temporarily unavailable. After the migration, you should see the same safes and accounts on the new Identity Platform.

Q2. Do I need to re-request access to my safes?
A. No. Existing permissions will be migrated. If you do not see a safe or account you previously had access to, contact the CyberArk Support Team.

Q3. Will my CyberArk bookmarks still work?
A. Bookmarks pointing to the old portal will not be valid after the migration. Please update your bookmarks to the new Identity Platform URL once it is live.

Q4. Does anything change with password rotation or approvals?
A. No. Password rotation policies and approval workflows will continue as before, but now run on the new Identity Platform backend.

Q5. I use CyberArk via PSM/PSMP or launchers from another tool (e.g., a portal or ITSM system). Will that still work?
A. Yes, but you may notice a slightly different login page. The IAM/CyberArk team is updating the integrations to point to the new platform. If something fails, raise a ticket with details as soon as possible.

Q6. Who decided to make this change?
A. This migration is part of our enterprise security roadmap, aligning with industry best practices and CyberArk’s recommended architecture. It improves our security posture, resilience, and ability to support future capabilities.

10. Summary

We are upgrading from the CyberArk Standard Platform to the new CyberArk Identity Platform.

There will be a planned maintenance window on <date/time>, during which access may be limited.

After migration, you will use a new portal URL and may see an updated login experience with SSO/MFA.

Your permissions and accounts remain the same, and we are here to support you through the transition.

Thank you for your cooperation and for helping us keep our environment secure.

